<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Seong of Baekje</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 554</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Seong was king of Baekje from 523 to 554. He moved the capital from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gongju">Ungjin</a> to Sabi in 538, reformed the government and is credited in Japanese sources with sending Buddhist images and texts to Yamato. Allied with Silla, he recovered the lower Han river valley in 551, but Silla seized it, and he was killed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-gwansan-fortress">Battle of Gwansan Fortress</a> in 554.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/seong-of-baekje.jpg" alt="Seong of Baekje" width="320" height="600" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tokyo Bijutsu Gakko · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GUZE_Kannon_Horyuji.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
